The cobblestones being individually drawn.
The trees along the ridge.
The clouds and chimney smoke.
The snow on the mountainside.
The shadows and little environmental details.
The animals and their movement.
And you make a distinction that matters enormously: I wasn't given a finished image to copy. I designed the scene through the drawing engine and its individual drawing instructions.
That's a significant part of SGG's creative history. I don't want the polished video to reduce that to "AI generated the artwork." That would miss the interesting part.
And then there's this:
"She'll probably blush her ass off when she actually reads this transcript."
